1
00:00:00,960 --> 00:00:01,840
Mark 12

2
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:05,340
And he began to speak to them in parables.

3
00:00:05,960 --> 00:00:10,780
A man planted a vineyard, and put a fence around it, and dug a pit for the winepress,

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,960
and built a tower, and leased it to tenants, and went into another country.

5
00:00:16,140 --> 00:00:20,720
When the season came, he sent a servant to the tenants to get from them some of the fruit

6
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:21,360
of the vineyard.

7
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,780
And they took him, and beat him, and sent him away empty-handed.

8
00:00:25,780 --> 00:00:31,420
Again he sent to them another servant, and they struck him on the head, and treated him

9
00:00:31,420 --> 00:00:32,060
shamefully.

10
00:00:32,580 --> 00:00:35,260
And he sent another, and him they killed.

11
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:40,200
And so with many others, some they beat, and some they killed.

12
00:00:41,380 --> 00:00:44,280
He had still one other, a beloved son.

13
00:00:44,940 --> 00:00:48,600
Finally he sent him to them, saying, They will respect my son.

14
00:00:49,340 --> 00:00:53,260
But those tenants said to one another, This is the heir.

15
00:00:53,260 --> 00:00:54,880
Come, let us kill him.

16
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:56,860
And the inheritance will be ours.

17
00:00:57,620 --> 00:01:01,220
And they took him, and killed him, and threw him out of the vineyard.

18
00:01:01,820 --> 00:01:04,000
What will the owner of the vineyard do?

19
00:01:04,720 --> 00:01:08,400
He will come and destroy the tenants, and give the vineyard to others.

20
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:11,220
Have you not read this scripture?

21
00:01:11,880 --> 00:01:15,940
The stone that the builders rejected has become the cornerstone.

22
00:01:16,520 --> 00:01:20,620
This was the Lord's doing, and it is marvelous in our eyes.

23
00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:24,760
And they were seeking to arrest him, but feared the people.

24
00:01:24,880 --> 00:01:28,080
For they perceived that he had told the parable against them.

25
00:01:28,460 --> 00:01:30,360
So they left him, and went away.

26
00:01:31,620 --> 00:01:36,180
And they sent to him some of the Pharisees, and some of the Herodians, to trap him in

27
00:01:36,180 --> 00:01:36,800
his talk.

28
00:01:37,140 --> 00:01:45,000
And they came and said to him, Teacher, we know that you are true, and do not care about

29
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:46,140
anyone's opinion.

30
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:52,740
For you are not swayed by appearances, but truly teach the way of God.

31
00:01:52,740 --> 00:01:54,660
Is it lawful?

32
00:01:54,660 --> 00:01:58,480
Is it lawful to pay taxes to Caesar, or not?

33
00:01:58,680 --> 00:02:01,840
Should we pay them, or should we not?

34
00:02:02,740 --> 00:02:07,920
But knowing their hypocrisy, he said to them, Why put me to the test?

35
00:02:08,580 --> 00:02:10,640
Bring me a denarius, and let me look at it.

36
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:16,600
And they brought one, and he said to them, Whose likeness and inscription is this?

37
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:20,440
They said to him, Caesar's.

38
00:02:21,020 --> 00:02:24,440
Jesus said to them, Render to Caesar the things that are in the Bible.

39
00:02:24,440 --> 00:02:24,520
Render to Caesar the things that are in the Bible.

40
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:24,640
Render to Caesar the things that are in the Bible.

41
00:02:24,640 --> 00:02:28,980
Render to God the things that are Caesar's, and to God the things that are God's.

42
00:02:29,700 --> 00:02:31,100
And they marveled at him.

43
00:02:31,660 --> 00:02:37,300
And Sadducees came to him, who say that there is no resurrection, and they asked him a question,

44
00:02:37,560 --> 00:02:45,360
saying, Teacher, Moses wrote for us that if a man's brother dies and leaves a wife, but

45
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:51,120
leaves no child, the man must take the widow and raise up offspring for his brother.

46
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:54,220
There were seven brothers.

47
00:02:54,640 --> 00:02:58,940
The first took a wife, and when he died, left no offspring.

48
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:03,320
And the second took her and died, leaving no offspring.

49
00:03:03,860 --> 00:03:05,420
And the third likewise.

50
00:03:06,360 --> 00:03:08,720
And the seven left no offspring.

51
00:03:09,420 --> 00:03:12,240
Last of all, the woman also died.

52
00:03:12,980 --> 00:03:19,100
In the resurrection, when they rise again, whose wife will she be?

53
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:21,660
For the seven had her as wife.

54
00:03:22,080 --> 00:03:23,360
Jesus said to them,

55
00:03:23,360 --> 00:03:25,920
Is this not the reason you are wrong?

56
00:03:26,300 --> 00:03:29,640
Because you know neither the Scriptures nor the power of God.

57
00:03:30,520 --> 00:03:34,460
For when they rise from the dead, they neither marry nor are given in marriage,

58
00:03:34,780 --> 00:03:36,440
but are like angels in heaven.

59
00:03:36,960 --> 00:03:40,960
And as for the dead being raised, have you not read in the book of Moses,

60
00:03:41,300 --> 00:03:44,600
in the passage about the bush, how God spoke to him, saying,

61
00:03:45,040 --> 00:03:49,680
I am the God of Abraham, and the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob?

62
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:52,640
He is not God of the dead,

63
00:03:52,640 --> 00:03:53,800
but of the living.

64
00:03:54,720 --> 00:03:56,240
You are quite wrong.

65
00:03:57,080 --> 00:04:00,600
And one of the scribes came up and heard them disputing with one another,

66
00:04:00,880 --> 00:04:03,580
and seeing that he answered them well, asked him,

67
00:04:04,300 --> 00:04:07,420
Which commandment is the most important of all?

68
00:04:08,120 --> 00:04:09,200
Jesus answered,

69
00:04:09,900 --> 00:04:11,200
The most important is,

70
00:04:11,920 --> 00:04:15,900
Hear, O Israel, the Lord our God, the Lord is one,

71
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:19,580
and you shall love the Lord your God with all your heart,

72
00:04:19,580 --> 00:04:22,400
and with all your soul, and with all your mind,

73
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:23,740
and with all your strength.

74
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:25,760
The second is this,

75
00:04:26,340 --> 00:04:28,420
You shall love your neighbor as yourself.

76
00:04:29,300 --> 00:04:32,260
There is no other commandment greater than these.

77
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:34,340
And the scribe said to him,

78
00:04:34,960 --> 00:04:36,420
You are right, teacher.

79
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:41,620
You have truly said that he is one, and there is no other besides him.

80
00:04:42,020 --> 00:04:45,760
And to love him with all the heart, and with all the understanding,

81
00:04:45,860 --> 00:04:49,540
and with all the strength, and to love one's neighbor as oneself,

82
00:04:49,700 --> 00:04:52,380
is much more than all whole burnt-out,

83
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:54,660
and is much more than all the offerings and sacrifices.

84
00:04:54,660 --> 00:04:58,040
And when Jesus saw that he answered wisely, he said to him,

85
00:04:58,740 --> 00:05:01,300
You are not far from the kingdom of God.

86
00:05:01,940 --> 00:05:05,600
And after that, no one dared to ask him any more questions.

87
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:10,160
And as Jesus taught in the temple, he said,

88
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:14,480
How can the scribe say that the Christ is the son of David?

89
00:05:15,080 --> 00:05:17,760
David himself in the Holy Spirit declared,

90
00:05:17,760 --> 00:05:19,680
The Lord said to my Lord,

91
00:05:20,060 --> 00:05:22,280
Sit at my right hand until I put your enemies,

92
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:23,160
under your feet.

93
00:05:23,620 --> 00:05:25,680
David himself calls him Lord.

94
00:05:26,240 --> 00:05:28,260
So how is he his son?

95
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:31,240
And the great throng heard him gladly.

96
00:05:31,820 --> 00:05:33,420
And in his teaching he said,

97
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:38,060
Beware of the scribes who like to walk around in long robes,

98
00:05:38,300 --> 00:05:40,180
and like greetings in the marketplaces,

99
00:05:40,500 --> 00:05:42,840
and have the best seats in the synagogues,

100
00:05:42,960 --> 00:05:45,400
and the places of honor at feasts,

101
00:05:45,400 --> 00:05:47,700
who devour widows' houses,

102
00:05:47,920 --> 00:05:49,940
and for a pretense make long prayers.

103
00:05:51,080 --> 00:05:52,260
They will receive,

104
00:05:52,400 --> 00:05:53,960
the greater condemnation.

105
00:05:55,660 --> 00:05:58,060
And he sat down opposite the treasury,

106
00:05:58,320 --> 00:06:01,020
and watched the people putting money into the offering box.

107
00:06:01,860 --> 00:06:03,640
Many rich people put in large sums,

108
00:06:04,080 --> 00:06:07,540
and a poor widow came and put in two small copper coins,

109
00:06:07,800 --> 00:06:08,580
which make a penny.

110
00:06:09,320 --> 00:06:12,060
And he called his disciples to him and said to them,

111
00:06:12,420 --> 00:06:14,160
Truly I say to you,

112
00:06:14,320 --> 00:06:19,000
this poor widow has put in more than all those who are contributing to the offering box.

113
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:21,800
For they all contributed out of their abundance,

114
00:06:22,400 --> 00:06:26,380
but she out of her poverty has put in everything she had,

115
00:06:26,740 --> 00:06:28,400
all she had to live on.

116
00:06:33,740 --> 00:06:38,740
The End

